    "data": {
      "text": "Court On Its Own Motion vs Uoi Through Secretary, Ministry Of \n... on 13 February, 2024 \nAuthor: Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora\nBench: Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora\n $~9 & 10\n * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi\n + W.P.(C) 7495/2010 and Cm Appl. 674\n 4764/2020\n Court On Its Own Motion \n Through: Mr. Ajay Pa\n Sriwas Nara\n Raj, Advoca\n \n Uoi Through Secretary, Ministry Of\n \n Through: Mr. T.P. Sin\n Mr. Rakesh C\n Tanvi, Advoc\n + W.P.(C) 2710/2014 and Cm Appl. 117\n Sharad Tiwari & Anr \n Through: \n \n \n \n The Govt. Of Nct Of Delhi \n Through: Mr. T.P. Si\n Mr. Anuj Ag\n Gnctd (Thro\n Arshya Sing\n Upadhyay, A\n Coram:\n Hon'Ble The Acting Chief Justice\n Hon'Ble Ms. Justice Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora\nThis is a digitally signed order. \nThe authenticity of the order can be re-verified from Delhi High Court Order Portal by s\nThe Order is downloaded from the Dhc Server on 15/02/2024 at 21:14:42\nCourt On Its Own Motion vs Uoi Through Secretary, Ministry Of ... on 13 February, 2024\nIndian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/43375629/\n1\n\n \n% 13.02.2024  CM APPL. 4765/2020(for exemption) in W.P.(C) 7495/2010 Allowed, subject to all just exceptions. Accordingly, the present application stands disposed of. W.P.(C) 7495/2010 & CM APPL. 4764/2020 W.P.(C) 2710/2014 & CM APPL. 11792/2015 1. Mr. Anuj Aggarwal, Advocate for GNCTD prays for an adjournment on the ground that he has been recently engaged. \n2. Learned counsel for Union of India states that he has filed an affidavit. However, the same is not on record. Let the same be brought on record forthwith. \n3. Since Food Safety Standards Authority of India ('FSSAI') is an apex body dealing with food safety standards, this Court directs FSSAI to prepare a roadmap for carrying out sampling and testing of food products in Delhi. \n4. Let the said plan be placed on record along with an affidavit so that the same can be executed and implemented by GNCTD.\n5. List on 08th May, 2024. \nACTING CHIEF JUSTICE MANMEET PRITAM SINGH ARORA, J FEBRUARY 13, 2024/hp This is a digitally signed order. \nThe authenticity of the order can be re-verified from Delhi High Court Order Portal by scanning the QR code shown above. The Order is downloaded from the DHC Server on 15/02/2024 at 21:14:42 Court On Its Own Motion vs Uoi Through Secretary, Ministry Of ... on 13 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/43375629/\n2",
